The document the README calls the port map was written before any of the port
existed and was never updated. It opened with "Status: compile layer only ...
the Bilibili session core behind it is a stub. Nothing here has been run on
Windows yet", listed livehime-core-stub.cpp as the Windows core, and its "what
is left, in order" section still asked for the Windows build, the core port, the
framework replacements, packaging and release automation — every one of which
shipped. A reader following the README to the port map was told nothing worked.

It now describes the port: the three layers and the C ABI seam between them, the
framework-for-framework table with the file each replacement lives in, what was
verified and against what, the seven things that are deliberately not done, and
the branding and config-isolation sections, which were already accurate and are
kept.

The verification section names the log events rather than asserting success, and
says plainly which of them rest on the account owner's word rather than on a log
line: the account owner took it end to end on 2026-09-26 — sign-in, danmaku,
going live, sending two danmaku and ending the live all appear in the log as
account state -> ready, danmaku status -> connected, stream state -> Starting ->
Live, live event -> danmakuSent and stream state -> Stopping -> liveStopped ->
Idle — while editing the title is confirmed by them but emits no titleUpdated in
that log.

Documentation only; no translation unit changes, so the released v0.2.10
binaries are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
